1. Objective
The objective of this introductory lab session was to become familiar with the course structure, syllabus, and evaluation
scheme of CSE 3154 Lab, understand the fundamentals and practical importance of GitHub for version control 
and project management, and gain an overview of the upcoming web programming topics.
2. Discussion and Key Learnings :
In this lab session, we discussed the overall curriculum and syllabus for the CSE 3154 Lab. 
The evaluation criteria and marks distribution for the course were clearly explained, 
giving a clear expectation of lab performance, assignments, reports, and assessments throughout the semester.
We learned how to create and navigate a GitHub profile as well as how to manage repositories and upload files. We also discussed 
the necessity of maintaining an active GitHub profile.
We were introduced to the roadmap for upcoming sessions, which will cover core web programming technologies 
including HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and PHP to build structured, styled, interactive, and dynamic web applications.
